  "term": "Stage 1 sleep",
  "definition": "Stage 1 sleep is the earliest, drowsy period at sleep onset, identified by characteristic EEG and behavioral changes. In older sleep-stage systems it was called Stage 1, but newer classification groups sleep onset and light sleep under N1–N2.",
